text:
maya: hey team :wave: I pushed a tiny Next.js starter that wires LlamaIndex + typed response shapes + i18n. seeing a weird auth/retry loop when deployed to edge. repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-typed-llama-starter
ashwin: can you paste the root error and the snippet where you call Redwood API? @maya :eyes:
maya: error from the edge logs: 
```
Request to /api/generate failed: 401 Unauthorized
redwood-sdk-js retrying request (attempt 3)
```
The API route is literally proxying to the SDK. here's the relevant bit (simplified):
```js
// pages/api/generate.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_API_KEY })
export default async function handler(req,res){
  const out = await client.chat.create({ model: 'l2-small', input: req.body.prompt })
  res.json(out)
}
```
Sophie: quick q: are you running that api route on the Edge runtime or Node server? If it's edge, env vars and secret scoping are different. Also using NEXT_PUBLIC_ pref means it's exposed to client. looks suspicious.
ashwin: yeah two things to check: 1) don't use NEXT_PUBLIC_* for server-side SDK keys, 2) sdk-js by default retries on many 5xx/429 and some auth flow; if the key is invalid you'll see repeated 401s. The retry layer doesn't know it's permanent. A minimal fix is to instantiate the client server-only and disable retries for 401. Example: 
```js
// server/utils/redwoodServerClient.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
export function getServerClient(){
  return new RedwoodClient({
    apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, // server-only secret
    retry: { statusCodes: [429, 502, 503], maxRetries: 2 } // exclude 401
  })
}
```
And then in the API route: 
```js
import { getServerClient } from '../../server/utils/redwoodServerClient'
const client = getServerClient()
// handle requests as before
```
maya: omg that was it — I accidentally followed a quickstart that used NEXT_PUBLIC_* in the example for convenience. Swapped to REDWOOD_API_KEY, adjusted retry config, redeployed to Edge and the 401/retry loop stopped. :+1:
sophie: can we add a lint/test to the sample repo to catch any env var that starts with NEXT_PUBLIC_ being used to construct a server client? would save future folks.
maya: opening PR now with fix + tiny test and a note in README about server-only keys. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-typed-llama-starter/pull/7
devex-bot: Created issue #342 in next-typed-llama-starter: "server client uses public env var, causes auth retries on edge"
maya: thanks all — closing loop. will also add a small eval harness to smoke-test generate route in CI so we catch regressions early.
